  <metadata>
    <id>carnac</id>
    <version>2.4.0</version>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/doggy8088/carnac/tree/dev/src/Chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <owners>willh</owners>
    <title>Carnac</title>
    <authors>Code52 and Carnac contributors</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://carnac.gh.miniasp.com/</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/doggy8088/carnac@0cf96733725787178d815e324a91dfc350fd8fc0/src/Carnac/carnac.png</iconUrl>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) Carnac contributors</copyright>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/doggy8088/carnac/blob/dev/LICENSE.md</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/doggy8088/carnac</projectSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/doggy8088/carnac#readme</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/doggy8088/carnac/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <tags>carnac keyboard keystroke overlay presentation screencast shortcuts</tags>
    <summary>A keystroke overlay that shows the keys and shortcuts you press, for presentations and screencasts.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
Carnac shows the keys and shortcuts you press as an on-screen overlay, so the people watching your talk, demo or screencast can follow along.

It labels shortcuts from bundled keymaps for Visual Studio, VS Code, ReSharper, Chrome, Kdenlive and NCrunch, supports your own YAML keymaps, and can be anchored to the top or bottom, left or right of any monitor.

This is the community-maintained fork of Code52's Carnac. The package downloads the official `Carnac-<version>-Setup.exe` from the project's GitHub Releases and runs it silently.

## Package notes

- The installer is per user: Carnac is installed into `%LocalAppData%\Programs\Carnac` for the account that runs Chocolatey and registered under that account's Programs and Features. It does not need administrator rights by itself.
- Carnac needs .NET Framework 4.5.2 or later, which is included in Windows 10 and Windows 11.
- Upgrading from the Chocolatey `carnac` 2.3.x packages removes the old Squirrel-based install from `%LocalAppData%\carnac` first, so only one copy of Carnac starts.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/doggy8088/carnac/releases/tag/v2.4.0</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
